public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Basic

/-!
# Associated primes of a Laurent extension

Let `A` be a commutative ring and let `B = A[T, T⁻¹]` be the Laurent polynomial ring over `A`.
This file computes the associated primes of a base-changed module along `A → B`:

`Ass_B(B ⊗_A M) = { 𝔭B : 𝔭 ∈ Ass_A(M) }`,

the inclusion `⊇` holding for every `A`-module `M` and the equality when `A` is Noetherian. The
extension `A → B` is free on the integer powers of `T`, hence faithfully flat, and a prime of `A`
stays prime in `B`; contracting back along `A → B` recovers the prime it came from, so the
displayed description is a bijection between `Ass_A(M)` and `Ass_B(B ⊗_A M)`.

The two halves are separated, because only the second is special to Laurent extensions.

The first is Stacks Tag 0312, already available as `associatedPrimes.tensorProduct_of_flat`: for
any ring map `A → B` with `B` flat over `A`,
`Ass_B(B ⊗_A M) = ⋃_{𝔭 ∈ Ass_A(M)} Ass_B(B / 𝔭B)`. Nothing here reproves it.

The second is that each of those unions has exactly one member. A prime `q` of a ring `R` is the
only associated prime of `R ⧸ q`, with no hypothesis on `R` whatever
(`assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton`): the annihilator of the class of `b` is `q` when `b ∉ q` and
is `⊤` — not prime — when `b ∈ q`. So it is enough to know that `𝔭B` is prime, and that is where
the Laurent structure enters: `B` is the localization of the polynomial ring `A[X]` at the powers
of `X` (`LaurentPolynomial.isLocalization`), `𝔭A[X]` is prime
(`Ideal.isPrime_map_C_of_isPrime`), and no power of `X` lies in `𝔭A[X]`, every coefficient of a
member of that ideal lying in `𝔭` while `X ^ n` has a coefficient `1`. A prime of the base disjoint
from the inverted monoid stays prime in a localization, and contracts back to itself.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton`: a prime `q` is the only
  associated prime of `R ⧸ q`, for any commutative ring `R`.
* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.isPrime_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial`: a prime of `A` stays
  prime in `A[T, T⁻¹]`.
* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.comap_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial`: and contracts back to
  itself.
* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.assStacks_tensor_eq_image`: the base-change description of the
  associated primes, for any flat extension in which primes stay prime.
* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.associatedPrimes_laurentPolynomial_tensor_eq_image`: the same
  for `A → A[T, T⁻¹]`, over a Noetherian ring, in Mathlib's `associatedPrimes` spelling on both
  sides.
* `Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes.mem_associatedPrimes_laurentPolynomial_iff`: the membership form
  — a prime of `A[T, T⁻¹]` is associated to `B ⊗_A M` exactly when it is generated by its
  contraction to `A` and that contraction is associated to `M`.

## Implementation notes

`Ass` is spelled two ways and the distinction is load-bearing. Mathlib's `associatedPrimes` asks
that a prime be the *radical* of the annihilator of an element; the Stacks source's `Ass`
(Tag 00LA) asks that it *be* that annihilator, and is a strictly smaller set in general. Tag 0312
is stated in the second spelling, so the statements that carry no Noetherian hypothesis are too,
written out as `{q | q.IsPrime ∧ ∃ w, (⊥ : Submodule R _).colon {w} = q}` because Tag 0312's own
`assStacks` abbreviation is `private` to its file. Over a Noetherian ring the two agree
(`isAssociatedPrime_iff`), which is the content of `assStacks_eq_associatedPrimes` and is how the
final statements are put into Mathlib's spelling on both sides — the base ring being Noetherian
and `A[T, T⁻¹]` therefore Noetherian too, by `isNoetherianRing_laurentPolynomial`.

`𝔭B` appears in Tag 0312 as `B ⧸ (𝔭.map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B B))`, which is the
ideal `𝔭B` itself only up to a propositional equality of submodules. Rewriting under the quotient
is not available, so `assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton` takes the submodule as a *parameter*
together with an equation identifying it, and is applied with that equation discharged by `simp`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0312](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0312)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00LA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00LA)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes

open Polynomial Submodule TensorProduct

/-! ### The associated primes of a quotient by a prime -/

section Quotient

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {J : Submodule R R}

/-- The annihilator of the class of `b` in `R ⧸ J` is `J` itself, for `J` prime and `b ∉ J`. -/
theorem colon_mk_eq_of_notMem (hq : Ideal.IsPrime J) {b : R} (hb : b ∉ J) :
    (⊥ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)).colon {Ideal.Quotient.mk J b} = J := by
  ext r
  rw [mem_colon_singleton, mem_bot, show r • (Ideal.Quotient.mk J b)
    = Ideal.Quotient.mk J (r * b) from rfl, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact ⟨fun h => (hq.mem_or_mem h).resolve_right hb, fun h => Ideal.mul_mem_right b J h⟩

/-- The annihilator of the class of `b` in `R ⧸ J` is everything when `b ∈ J`. -/
theorem colon_mk_eq_top_of_mem {b : R} (hb : b ∈ J) :
    (⊥ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)).colon {Ideal.Quotient.mk J b} = ⊤ := by
  ext r
  rw [mem_colon_singleton, mem_bot, show r • (Ideal.Quotient.mk J b)
    = Ideal.Quotient.mk J (r * b) from rfl, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact ⟨fun _ => Submodule.mem_top, fun _ => Ideal.mul_mem_left J r hb⟩

/-- **A prime `q` is the only prime of `R` associated to `R ⧸ q`**, for any commutative ring `R`
and in the annihilator spelling of Stacks Tag 00LA. No Noetherian hypothesis is needed: the
annihilator of the class of `b` is `q` for `b ∉ q` and `⊤` for `b ∈ q`, and `⊤` is not prime.

The quotient is taken by a submodule `J` supplied with an equation `J = q`, so that the statement
can be applied where `q` arises as `𝔭.map (algebraMap A B) • ⊤` rather than as an ideal on the
nose. -/
theorem assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton {q : Ideal R} (hq : q.IsPrime) (hJ : J = q) :
    {P : Ideal R | P.IsPrime ∧ ∃ w : R ⧸ J,
      (⊥ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)).colon {w} = P} = {q} := by
  subst hJ
  have hmem : Ideal.IsPrime J ∧ ∃ w : R ⧸ J,
      (⊥ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)).colon {w} = J := by
    have h1 : (1 : R) ∉ J := fun h => hq.ne_top (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ h isUnit_one)
    exact ⟨hq, Ideal.Quotient.mk J 1, colon_mk_eq_of_notMem hq h1⟩
  ext P
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, fun h => h ▸ hmem⟩
  rintro ⟨hP, w, hw⟩
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective w
  by_cases hb : b ∈ J
  · rw [colon_mk_eq_top_of_mem hb] at hw
    exact absurd (hw ▸ hP) (by simp [Ideal.isPrime_iff])
  · rw [colon_mk_eq_of_notMem hq hb] at hw
    exact hw.symm

/-- Over a Noetherian ring the annihilator spelling of `Ass` (Stacks Tag 00LA) agrees with
Mathlib's `associatedPrimes`, which takes the radical. -/
theorem assStacks_eq_associatedPrimes [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] :
    {q : Ideal R | q.IsPrime ∧ ∃ w : M, (⊥ : Submodule R M).colon {w} = q}
      = associatedPrimes R M := by
  ext q
  rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, AssociatedPrimes.mem_iff, isAssociatedPrime_iff]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨h1, w, h2⟩ => ⟨h1, w, h2.symm⟩, fun ⟨h1, w, h2⟩ => ⟨h1, w, h2.symm⟩⟩

end Quotient

/-! ### Base change along a flat extension in which primes stay prime -/

section BaseChange

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Flat A B]
  (hmap : ∀ p : Ideal A, p.IsPrime → (p.map (algebraMap A B)).IsPrime)
  (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]

include hmap in
/-- **The extension of an associated prime is an associated prime of the base change**, along any
flat extension `A → B` in which primes stay prime. No Noetherian hypothesis; `Ass` is the
annihilator spelling of Stacks Tag 00LA. -/
theorem image_assStacks_subset_assStacks_tensor :
    (fun p : Ideal A => p.map (algebraMap A B)) ''
        {p : Ideal A | p.IsPrime ∧ ∃ m : M, (⊥ : Submodule A M).colon {m} = p}
      ⊆ {q : Ideal B | q.IsPrime ∧
          ∃ w : B ⊗[A] M, (⊥ : Submodule B (B ⊗[A] M)).colon {w} = q} := by
  rintro q ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
  refine (associatedPrimes.tensorProduct_of_flat (R := A) (S := B) (M := M) (N := B)).1 ?_
  refine Set.mem_biUnion hp ?_
  rw [assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton (hmap p hp.1) (by simp)]
  rfl

include hmap in
/-- **The associated primes of a base change are exactly the extensions of the associated primes
of the module**, along a flat extension `A → B` of a Noetherian ring in which primes stay prime.

`Ass_B` is in the annihilator spelling of Stacks Tag 00LA; see
`associatedPrimes_tensor_eq_image` for the form with Mathlib's `associatedPrimes` on both sides. -/
theorem assStacks_tensor_eq_image [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    {q : Ideal B | q.IsPrime ∧
        ∃ w : B ⊗[A] M, (⊥ : Submodule B (B ⊗[A] M)).colon {w} = q}
      = (fun p : Ideal A => p.map (algebraMap A B)) '' associatedPrimes A M := by
  rw [(associatedPrimes.tensorProduct_of_flat (R := A) (S := B) (M := M) (N := B)).2 ‹_›]
  have key : ∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes A M,
      {Q : Ideal B | Q.IsPrime ∧ ∃ w : B ⧸ (p.map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B B)),
        (⊥ : Submodule B (B ⧸ (p.map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B B)))).colon {w} = Q}
        = {p.map (algebraMap A B)} :=
    fun p hp => assStacks_quotient_eq_singleton (hmap p hp.1) (by simp)
  ext q
  refine ⟨fun hq => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨p, hp, hq⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp hq
    rw [key p hp] at hq
    exact ⟨p, hp, hq.symm⟩
  · rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    exact Set.mem_biUnion hp (by rw [key p hp]; rfl)

include hmap in
/-- `assStacks_tensor_eq_image` with Mathlib's `associatedPrimes` on both sides, which needs `B`
Noetherian as well as `A`. -/
theorem associatedPrimes_tensor_eq_image [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B] :
    associatedPrimes B (B ⊗[A] M)
      = (fun p : Ideal A => p.map (algebraMap A B)) '' associatedPrimes A M := by
  rw [← assStacks_eq_associatedPrimes (R := B) (B ⊗[A] M), assStacks_tensor_eq_image hmap M]

end BaseChange

/-! ### The Laurent extension -/

section Laurent

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A]

/-- `A → A[X] → A[T, T⁻¹]` is `A → A[T, T⁻¹]`. -/
theorem algebraMap_laurent_comp_C :
    (algebraMap A[X] (LaurentPolynomial A)).comp Polynomial.C
      = algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A) := by
  ext a
  simp [LaurentPolynomial.algebraMap_eq_toLaurent, ← LaurentPolynomial.C_eq_algebraMap]

/-- No power of `X` lies in the extension of a prime to `A[X]`: every coefficient of a member of
that ideal lies in the prime, while `X ^ n` has a coefficient `1`. -/
theorem disjoint_powers_X_map_C {p : Ideal A} (hp : p.IsPrime) :
    Disjoint (Submonoid.powers (Polynomial.X : A[X]) : Set A[X])
      (Ideal.map (Polynomial.C : A →+* A[X]) p : Set A[X]) := by
  rw [Set.disjoint_left]
  rintro a ⟨n, rfl⟩ ha
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_map_C_iff] at ha
  have := ha n
  simp only [Polynomial.coeff_X_pow] at this
  exact hp.ne_top (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (by simpa using this) isUnit_one)

/-- **A prime ideal of `A` stays prime in the Laurent extension `A[T, T⁻¹]`.** -/
theorem isPrime_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial (p : Ideal A) [hp : p.IsPrime] :
    (p.map (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A))).IsPrime := by
  have h := IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint
    (Submonoid.powers (Polynomial.X : A[X])) (LaurentPolynomial A)
    (Ideal.map (Polynomial.C : A →+* A[X]) p) Ideal.isPrime_map_C_of_isPrime
    (disjoint_powers_X_map_C hp)
  rwa [Ideal.map_map, algebraMap_laurent_comp_C] at h

/-- **Contracting the extension of a prime back along `A → A[T, T⁻¹]` recovers the prime.** -/
theorem comap_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial (p : Ideal A) [hp : p.IsPrime] :
    (p.map (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A))).comap
      (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A)) = p := by
  have h := IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint
    (Submonoid.powers (Polynomial.X : A[X])) (LaurentPolynomial A)
    (I := Ideal.map (Polynomial.C : A →+* A[X]) p) Ideal.isPrime_map_C_of_isPrime
    (disjoint_powers_X_map_C hp)
  rw [Ideal.under_def] at h
  rw [← algebraMap_laurent_comp_C, ← Ideal.map_map, ← Ideal.comap_comap, h]
  ext a
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_map_C_iff]
  refine ⟨fun hh => by simpa using hh 0, fun hh n => ?_⟩
  rcases eq_or_ne n 0 with rfl | hn
  · simpa using hh
  · simp [Polynomial.coeff_C, hn]

/-- The Laurent extension of a Noetherian ring is Noetherian, being a localization of a polynomial
ring in one variable. -/
theorem isNoetherianRing_laurentPolynomial [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    IsNoetherianRing (LaurentPolynomial A) :=
  IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing (Submonoid.powers (Polynomial.X : A[X])) _ inferInstance

variable (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]

/-- **The extension of an associated prime of `M` is an associated prime of
`A[T, T⁻¹] ⊗_A M`**, for every `A`-module `M` and with no hypothesis on `A`. `Ass` is the
annihilator spelling of Stacks Tag 00LA. -/
theorem image_assStacks_subset_assStacks_tensor_laurentPolynomial :
    (fun p : Ideal A => p.map (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A))) ''
        {p : Ideal A | p.IsPrime ∧ ∃ m : M, (⊥ : Submodule A M).colon {m} = p}
      ⊆ {q : Ideal (LaurentPolynomial A) | q.IsPrime ∧
          ∃ w : LaurentPolynomial A ⊗[A] M,
            (⊥ : Submodule (LaurentPolynomial A) (LaurentPolynomial A ⊗[A] M)).colon {w} = q} :=
  image_assStacks_subset_assStacks_tensor
    (fun p hp => isPrime_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial (hp := hp) p) M

/-- **The associated primes of `A[T, T⁻¹] ⊗_A M` are exactly the extensions `𝔭·A[T, T⁻¹]` of the
associated primes `𝔭` of `M`**, for `A` Noetherian. -/
theorem associatedPrimes_laurentPolynomial_tensor_eq_image [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    associatedPrimes (LaurentPolynomial A) (LaurentPolynomial A ⊗[A] M)
      = (fun p : Ideal A => p.map (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A))) ''
          associatedPrimes A M :=
  have := isNoetherianRing_laurentPolynomial (A := A)
  associatedPrimes_tensor_eq_image
    (fun p hp => isPrime_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial (hp := hp) p) M

/-- **The membership form.** A prime of `A[T, T⁻¹]` is associated to `A[T, T⁻¹] ⊗_A M` exactly
when it is generated by its contraction to `A` and that contraction is an associated prime of `M`;
and then the contraction is recovered from it. This is the form in which the comparison is used to
move an associated prime between a graded ring and the degree-zero part of a localization. -/
theorem mem_associatedPrimes_laurentPolynomial_iff [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {q : Ideal (LaurentPolynomial A)} :
    q ∈ associatedPrimes (LaurentPolynomial A) (LaurentPolynomial A ⊗[A] M)
      ↔ q.comap (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A)) ∈ associatedPrimes A M
        ∧ q = (q.comap (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A))).map
            (algebraMap A (LaurentPolynomial A)) := by
  rw [associatedPrimes_laurentPolynomial_tensor_eq_image M]
  refine ⟨?_, fun ⟨h1, h2⟩ => ⟨_, h1, h2.symm⟩⟩
  rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
  have : p.IsPrime := hp.1
  rw [comap_map_algebraMap_laurentPolynomial p]
  exact ⟨hp, rfl⟩

end Laurent

end Stacks.LaurentAssociatedPrimes

end
